        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Measurement of an organism&#39;s, organ&#39;s, tissue&#39;s or cell&#39;s capacity to respond, such as by a change in activity, state or condition, to acetylcholine (ACh), the ester of acetic acid and choline with chemical formula CH3C=OO(CH2)2-N(+)-(CH3)3 and IUPAC name 2-acetoxy-N,N,N-trimethylethanaminium, which acts as a neurotransmitter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
